# Runtime dependencies of Riot Commander - the HUMAN-EDITED source of
# requirements.txt. Exact `==` pins of what RC's own tracked source imports,
# no hashes (tests/test_requirements_currency_rm515.py reads this file).
#
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file: every package, transitive ones
# included, pinned to an exact version AND to the sha256 of every file PyPI
# serves for it, so `pip install -r requirements.txt` (install.bat) runs in
# hash-checking mode and refuses anything else. Never hand-edit
# requirements.txt: change a pin here, then regenerate from the repo root with:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.11 --generate-hashes --output-file requirements.txt
#
# --universal + --python-version 3.11 resolve ONE file for every platform and
# every Python from 3.11 up: the embedded runtime (python-embed, 3.11), CI and
# the README floor (3.12), 3.13, and the operator's runtime (3.14). Without
# --upgrade, uv keeps every version already pinned in requirements.txt, so a
# regeneration after one edit here moves only what that edit forces.
#
# The hashed CI install sets in .github/ci/ include this file too (see the .in
# beside each); after a pin change here regenerate them with the commands in
# their headers, or ci.yml's "hashed CI install sets agree" step goes red.

